    {
      "ref": "01KHYAV7",
      "text": "Surface ACP usage/cost data in ralph session stats — after SDK bump to 0.14.x, new Usage/UsageUpdate/Cost types are available. Could add token usage per iteration and cumulative cost to session log stats and web UI. The usage_update SessionUpdate variant fires during sessions with context window utilization data.\n\n---\n\nIMPORTANT FINDING: Neither claude-agent-acp nor codex-acp actually emit usage_update events or populate PromptResponse.usage. Both have raw token data available but discard it. kynetic-bot works around this by scraping /context stderr (fragile regex). Upstream PR to claude-agent-acp is highest-value path — Anthropic API stream events contain usage data, just needs wiring to ACP protocol.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T20:11:19.317Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYDW5",
      "text": "Explore CLAUDE_CODE_SIMPLE mode for ralph loops — sets minimal system prompt with only Bash, file read, and file edit tools. Disables MCP tools, attachments, hooks, and CLAUDE.md. Could reduce token overhead and speed up startup, but ralph would need to inject all project context (AGENTS.md rules, spec-first workflow, kspec conventions) into the prompt itself instead of relying on Claude Code's built-in mechanisms. Tradeoff: simpler/faster agent vs ralph becomes responsible for all context bootstrapping. Ref: anthropics/claude-code#27019",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T21:04:14.935Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
    {
      "ref": "01KHYFD9",
      "text": "Ralph worktree isolation for task work — spawn each agent in a git worktree under a gitignored .worktrees/ dir for branch isolation. Pattern proven in kynetic-internal with jj workspaces. Key insight: kspec resolves .kspec/ via git root, but worktrees return their own root from rev-parse --show-toplevel. Solution: ralph sets KSPEC_SPEC_DIR to point to main tree's .kspec/ when spawning agents (env var already exists for batch mode). Benefits: isolated branches per task, parallel agent work, trivial cleanup of failed work, clean main branch. Unknowns: shadow branch commands from worktree context, git config inheritance, worktree lifecycle management in ralph.",
      "created_at": "2026-02-20T21:31:05.321Z",
      "tags": [],
      "added_by": "@claude",
      "triaged": true,
      "triage_action": "defer"
    },
